[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Affine behavioral source temperature slice

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Acceptance target is unchanged original regression/misc/asrc-tc-1.cir:
complete original OP and AC requests, every mapped physical signal, original
assertions and stock-ngspice full program, without weaker bounds. Reuse the
adopted generated metadata, affine source preparation, typed VCCS/VCVS/source
emission, per-point compiler and ordered reporting. No numerical kernel,
expression parser, dependency or production legacy runtime is added. Retained
reuse decisions are in docs/spicesharp-evaluation.md. Pinned RSpice builder/
behavioral.rs guides finite TC1/TC2 scaling; no source is copied.

Plan: reproduce baseline refusal; add positive/negative root temperature,
affine coefficient and failure-only early-exit regressions; preserve generated
metadata and strict profile refusals; compile one finite literal root .temp
only for qualified linear circuits; scale affine offsets and all coefficients;
retain existing OP/AC result identity checks; verify original assertions,
negative assertions, coverage, properties, mutation and real StrictDoc parsing.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BEHAVIOR-TEMPERATURE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Finite requested affine behavioral temperature scaling
STATEMENT: >>>
Requested affine B voltage and current preparation shall preserve generated
TC1/TC2 parameter ranges, evaluate coefficients in the retained instance
environment and multiply the whole affine relation by 1+TC1*dT+TC2*dT*dT,
where dT is Celsius minus the qualified nominal temperature of 27 C. Finite
zero and negative factors shall preserve their mathematical sign. Nonfinite
factors or any scaled coefficient shall fail atomically with
invalid_behavior_temperature_factor; duplicate or unknown
attributes shall refuse. The strict public affine profile shall retain its
prior refusal of additional physical attributes.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: BehavioralSourceSyntax and BehavioralSourceLowering.
Verification: BehavioralTemperatureTests; evidence/behavioral-temperature.json.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-REQUESTED-ROOT-TEMPERATURE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bounded literal root operating temperature
STATEMENT: >>>
Requested preparation shall admit at most one source-located literal root
.temp above absolute zero and publish the selected Celsius temperature. It
shall apply that value to parameter evaluation, passive and affine behavioral
preparation. Nondefault temperatures shall refuse unqualified nonlinear or
semiconductor circuits, conflicting default-temperature options and control
constant exports. A DC temperature sweep shall explicitly override the root
operating temperature at each sweep point. Multiple, nested, nonliteral or
invalid temperature directives shall not be silently omitted.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: DeclarationExtraction and RequestedAnalysis.Prepare.
Verification: BehavioralTemperatureTests; evidence/behavioral-temperature.json.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONTROL-EARLY-FAILURE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Conditional reporting failure before a later analysis
STATEMENT: >>>
Ordered reporting preparation may admit conditional quit 1 before a later
unconditional analysis. An active failure shall return status 1 before binding
later reporting plots and shall prevent original-program agreement. Early
successful exits and unconditional early exits shall remain refused. Required
physical results shall still be complete and validated before ordered reporting;
this bounded postprocessing contract does not promise lazy physical dispatch.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: OrderedControlPreparation and ControlVectorExecution.
Verification: BehavioralTemperatureTests and authored negative original-program
fixture; evidence/behavioral-temperature.json.
<<<
